ut a universal grammar may know five  languages ten languages they don't know  three thousand  six thousand languages  so um and and i understand too that that  one of uh  chomsky's reasons for assuming there was  a universal grammar was otherwise he  said how could you explain that children  uh learn to speak so quickly well they  don't learn to speak so quickly they  spend an awful long time hearing the  language they're even exposed to the  language in the womb  so  and when they start speaking they  stumble  and they gradually through trial and  error  you know pick up on the pattern of the  language that surrounds them  which you know could be  spoken in more complete sentences  in some languages or in some  environments or could be spoken in very  basic  forms of communication where a lot of  other stuff  outside the language is understood  so  i guess what i'm saying is that i enjoy  languages i enjoy learning them uh when  i start new languages i will at link  we're going to introduce new languages  uh czech dodge you know indonesian  i just want to go at them  and and uh read and listen and and look  up with their little uh you know with  the online dictionary create flash cards  um  yeah explanations will help me because  i'm an adult  but my ability to understand the  explanations is limited so we are going  to introduce notes pages so that our  members can provide some explanation and  i may refer to that and and and then go  back and refer to it again and it'll be  part of the whole process of gradually  absorbing the language without parsing  without morphology without whatever else  was in that thing and uh and so  you know and when i pick up i don't know  like the language instinct and i see  these diagrams that so i'll just happen  to have it here you know all these  diagrams and stuff like that i tell you  my eyes just  glass over  uh  you know s  dash np vp sense can consist of a noun  phrase and a verb phrase do these terms  actually mean anything in in terms of  other languages this was the thing i  found learning chinese a bunch of  grammatical terms from from western  european languages that had had no  relevance for for japanese and chinese  anyway enough this is quite a long one  and um i will leave you with that and i  look forward to the continuing comments  and i must say that some of the  linguistics i don't want to knock  linguistics and everyone who studies  linguistics i think it's very  interesting to study the history of  different languages and how they're  related and how they develop  and uh and if people are interested  they're interested in it so it's perfect  legitimate in that sense it's just that  uh when people come at me and say that  you can't learn the language if you  don't parse if you don't know what  phonemes and morphemes and all this  other stuff  uh r  is are these things are  then you know and you shouldn't be  starting off on how to learn languages  because you're a fool and you're  anti-intellectual and stuff so i  appreciate the  linguists in the sense of linguistics  specialist who have commented in a in a  nice tone uh here at my uh at my uh  youtube channel and i look forward to  seeing further comments thank you

